      "quotableDescriptiveWitnessInChapter": false,
      "primaryEvidence": [
        {
          "unitId": "s0086",
          "zh": "馮衍字敬通，京兆杜陵人也。",
          "literal": "Feng Yan, courtesy name Jingtong, was a man of Duling in the metropolitan region of Jingzhao."
        },
        {
          "unitId": "s0087",
          "zh": "祖野王，元帝時為大鴻臚。",
          "literal": "His grandfather Yewang, in the time of Yuandi, was Grand Herald.",
          "idiomatic": "His grandfather Feng Yewang had been grand herald under Emperor Yuan."
        },
        {
          "unitId": "s0088",
          "zh": "衍幼有奇才，年九歲，能誦《詩》，至二十而博通群書。"
        }
      ],
      "findings": [
        "s0087 祖野王，元帝時為大鴻臚 names only Feng Yan's grandfather 野王 (p029, kinship term 祖). It contains no surface, kinship phrase or personal name for Feng Yan's father.",
        "p087 has 0 mentions and 0 surfaces. Its only name is an English descriptive-kinship label \"Father of Feng Yan\" with no Chinese form. Its own mentionException says \"chapter names Feng Yan's grandfather ... but not Yan's father; created to complete the grandfather–father–son kinship path.\"",
        "A scan of the Feng Yan section (s0086 onward) for 先人/先君/先將軍/先父/家君/父/考 and English \"his/my (late) father\" finds only allusions (逢醜父 s0099, 孫林父 s0171) and generic 父子/君父 (s0133, s0139, s0202). None refers to Feng Yan's father.",
        "Both p087 attestations cite sourceDate text \"元帝至莽\", which does not occur anywhere in the chapter source (0 occurrences). The interval BC 48–AD 23 was inferred, not quoted.",
        "The grandfather–grandson path is already captured without the intermediary: compact claim index 94 (normalized houhanshu:031:c0383) is p029 ancestor-of p028, 祖/grandfather, generationDistance 2, line paternal, explicit, evidence s0087.",
        "The canonical person per_B9GFH90PRDFQ9TEB324J is stableCanonicalPersonId(\"houhanshu:032:p014\"), not p087 (which derives per_XBKJGRR7XFFNZ0FFT447). It has established, quotable primary evidence in houhanshu/032 s0030 先將軍葬渭陵 (\"My late father, the general, lay buried at Weiling\"), the transport witness the reviewer cited. Removing the 031 placeholder does not erase Feng Yan's father from the corpus; it removes only an unwitnessed membership."
      ],
